implementationPlan.description:
FIX canonicalProjectPath in scripts/local-runner/vm-control.mjs (~line 31) by porting the landed proxy rule (packages/moe-proxy/src/utils.ts comparableProjectPath, task-ea57601d). The daemon's own copy (packages/moe-daemon/src/index.ts ~99) already follows it. The body becomes:

```js
  const raw = projectPath.trim();
  if (/^[a-zA-Z]:[\\/]/.test(raw)) return windowsDrive(raw);
  const resolved = path.resolve(raw);
  const wsl = /^\/mnt\/([a-zA-Z])(?:\/(.*))?$/.exec(process.platform === 'win32' ? path.posix.normalize(raw) : resolved);
  if (wsl) {
    const rest = (wsl[2] ?? '').replace(/\/+$/, '');
    return `${wsl[1]}:${rest ? `/${rest}` : ''}`.toLowerCase();
  }
  return /^[a-zA-Z]:[\\/]/.test(resolved) ? windowsDrive(resolved) : process.platform === 'win32' ? resolved.toLowerCase() : resolved;
```

Replace the stale comment 'Both special forms are matched on the raw string...'. The new comment says:
- a drive path is matched raw, because path.resolve treats it as relative off Windows;
- /mnt/<d> is matched only after normalizing: path.resolve on POSIX, path.posix.normalize of the raw string on win32, where path.resolve would prefix the cwd drive.
Also point the doc line at the fixed proxy rule (and the daemon's index.ts twin).

No import changes. local-runner-bundle.test.mjs checks the import closure, and path is already imported.

Error handling and compatibility:
- ownedLedgerDir's validation (blank, control characters) and the state-dir-inside-project refusal are unchanged.
- Every already-canonical input keeps its key and ledger hash: VC-L2's literals prove it.
- Only mis-keyed inputs (relative, or non-normalized /mnt) change key, which is the fix.

Run `node --test scripts/tests/local-runner-vm-control.test.mjs`: all green.

planningNotes.codebaseInsights:
There are three copies of the project-path canonicalizer:
- daemon packages/moe-daemon/src/index.ts comparableProjectPath (fixed: normalize first);
- proxy packages/moe-proxy/src/utils.ts (fixed by ea57601d);
- scripts/local-runner/vm-control.mjs canonicalProjectPath (raw-string /mnt; this task).

ownedLedgerDir hashes the canonical string: sha256, first 32 hex, under MOE_RUNNER_STATE_DIR or ~/.moe/runner-state. readDaemonInfo compares canonical forms of daemon.json projectPath and the caller's path.

The proxy fix's tests emulate win32 by flipping process.platform and stubbing path.resolve with path.win32.resolve('C:\\work', ...). node:test's t.mock.method can do the same to node:path's default export and to process.cwd.
